From 70212d3f0633e56e40c89f2e9031e34c0adbd556 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Karim Baba <karim.sf09@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 10:21:25 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] Peek the notch when a WARDEN agent needs you

WARDEN's own menu-bar panel used to open for this. With the section
running that was the same alert twice, one covering the other.

WardenAttentionMonitor holds WARDEN's /attention stream natively, next to
the web view rather than inside it: the page's event stream is open only
while the section is on screen, and the whole point of an alert is that
it arrives when you are not looking at the notch. Holding that stream is
also what tells WARDEN to stay down, so the toggle in Settings hands the
alert straight back and there is no state where both speak or neither.

The peek keeps the three properties that made WARDEN's summon a
notification rather than an interruption: it fires on the transition, it
takes no focus, and it leaves after six seconds unless the pointer
arrived, which is the operator answering it.

Also: a wardenHost script-message handler, so a globe click can put the
panel away at once instead of leaving the notch open over the terminal
window it just asked for.
